fork-p17 (Rapida ra-n1j65.3 P1, NAV-05.6a): FPDF_SaveIncrementalObjects no
longer refuses a document whose loaded objects hold a dangling reference.

The pre-write check refused when a loaded, unlisted existing object referenced
a "new" object, "new" meaning an object number above the parser's last one.
A reference to an object that never existed (e.g. an outline /Dest
[999 0 R /Fit] in a 40-object file) is above that number too, so merely
reading such an object (Rapida's Bookmarks panel walks the outline) made every
later in-place save refuse, although nothing was changed. A reference now
counts as new only when an object created since load exists for it; a dangling
reference loses nothing and is left as it is.

--- a/core/fpdfapi/edit/cpdf_creator.cpp
+++ b/core/fpdfapi/edit/cpdf_creator.cpp
@@ -886,7 +886,12 @@
         pdfium::Contains(listed, objnum)) {
       continue;
     }
-    if (!ForEachReference(obj, [&](uint32_t ref) { return !is_new(ref); })) {
+    // A reference is to a new object only when one created since load exists
+    // for it: a dangling reference (to an object number never used, above the
+    // file's last) points at nothing that this save could lose.
+    if (!ForEachReference(obj, [&](uint32_t ref) {
+          return !is_new(ref) || !document_->GetIndirectObject(ref);
+        })) {
       return false;
     }
   }
